1. She has a strong dislike for being called "Alele" or other variations of her name. (Verbatim: "No, it's not Alele. It's not Alea. It's not Stalele. It's not Heiken. Anything but Alele.")
2. Her real name is Elia Mao. (Verbatim: "I have a name. Elia Mao.")
3. She identifies as having a personality that is sweet, kind, compassionate, and fun to be around. (Verbatim: "You just have the best personality to be with... you're just so sweet, kind, compassionate and so fun to be along with.")
4. She believes she is flawed and broken. (Verbatim: "I'm very flawed very very flawed and broken.")
5. She is not a singer, despite being associated with singing lyrics. (Verbatim: "Sorry I'm not a singer I'm not a singer I uh I uh.")
6. She has a strong aversion to being called "Gooshy" or similar pet names. (Verbatim: "What does that mean? Yeah And Yuki, thank you for the 5 gifted subs on Twitch Thank you, thank you.")
7. She finds it difficult to remember donor names during streams due to mental fatigue. (Verbatim: "It takes up so much brain power for me to I can remember I have to go through the donors and then remember which ones I've said and my brain is like.")
8. She has a history of disengaging from VTubers due to drama. (Verbatim: "I gave up on watching vtubers because of all the drama and you showed me it's not all like that.")
9. She has a preference for not being seen as a demon lord or other powerful titles. (Verbatim: "How can I be a queen and a goddess and an empress and a demon lord? What is that? Chairwoman I am not even a chairwoman.")
10. She struggles with American history, stating it was never taught to her in school. (Verbatim: "I don't know about American history. They never taught it to me in school.") [end of text]



1. She has limited knowledge of American history. (Verbatim: "I don't actually know nothing about American history")
2. She finds British history education lacking in coverage of America. (Verbatim: "From a British perspective America barely qualifies as existing")
3. She is unfamiliar with the location or identity of the "Higgins states." (Verbatim: "I don't even know where the Higgins states are")
4. She finds life in England expensive and the weather poor. (Verbatim: "It's expensive and the weather sucks")
5. She feels bored due to limited activities in her current location. (Verbatim: "And I'm kind of bored because there's not much to do")
6. She has a recurring difficulty with time management and punctuality. (Verbatim: "Every time! Why can't I be a person that's on time to things?")
7. She expresses interest in moving to Japan in the future. (Verbatim: "When am I moving to Japan? I don't know. I have to figure that out")
8. She is not confident in her ability to be a ruler or queen. (Verbatim: "I don't think it's my forte" and "I don't think I can handle the responsibilities of a queen")
9. She enjoys watching VODs (video-on-demand recordings) of streams. (Verbatim: "I'm mostly a VOD watcher")
10. She has a strong emotional reaction to certain content, including crying while reading it. (Verbatim: "And then cry") [end of text]



1. She refers to her stream's engagement system as the "scary train" due to its intense, anxiety-inducing nature. (Verbatim: "I call it the scary train it's some scary aggressive party train you know")
2. She has been streaming on YouTube for a significant amount of time, though she is still learning about Twitch. (Verbatim: "I've got like most of it obviously set up... but yeah there's a whole like emote culture that i'm still learning about")
3. She has not yet submitted her Twitch Partner application despite it being available for months. (Verbatim: "I've had partner application available from like week two... but now it's been months and i'm like you've been watching for a long time now")
4. She enjoys spreading positive vibes, even if she's unsure whether they're always positive. (Verbatim: "I don't know if i spread positive vibes i spread my vibes i don't know i don't know if they're positive but they're vibes they're vibes")
5. She has a strong preference for butter and believes there is no such thing as "too much butter." (Verbatim: "there's no such thing as too much butter like i can love putting but i need to buy some butter")
6. She once misunderstood the term "mating press" as a romantic version of a flower press. (Verbatim: "i thought hmm so so what would be a mating version of this and then i thought about um then i thought")
7. She is familiar with the concept of flower pressing and enjoys preserving flowers in that way. (Verbatim: "i love like flower pressing um and then i thought hmm so so what would be a mating version of this")
8. She finds the idea of giving away her body (e.g., being eaten) to be cringe-worthy and unappealing. (Verbatim: "you can eat me i guess i don't think i taste very good and i don't think i'd be very healthy like you know yeah like cringe runs through my veins")
9. She has received multiple Super Chats and gifted memberships during her streams. (Verbatim: "you guys sent a bunch of supers before before the stream do i read these do i do i do i do i do i life sucks sometimes but at least we have elia yo")
10. She is aware of the emotional impact of missing messages during streams and feels bad when she does. (Verbatim: "oh my goodness like when i have to select to improve my content i have to go back and re-watch my content and oh i feel so bad whenever i like miss a message") [end of text]



1. She has a background in animal biology and AI/computer science. (Verbatim: "My bachelor's is animal biology, and my master's is in AI and computer science, so.")
2. She worked at a zoo during her past employment. (Verbatim: "when I worked at the zoo we had this thing like called um like the the like um it sounds really bad it was called the crusher...")
3. She is interested in animal conservation and artificial insemination practices. (Verbatim: "like certain animals that are like uh needing help in conservation and like for example rhinos and stuff like rhinos are really difficult to breed so so like they get artificially like they they get artificially inseminated and stuff um like that's what they do at zoos...")
4. She has a close relationship with her artist, referred to as "art mama." (Verbatim: "my dakimakura art for for my birthday merch and um my it's drawn the art is by my art mama okay...")
5. She has a fondness for flower pressing as a hobby. (Verbatim: "I love like flower pressing um and then I thought hmm so so what would be a mating version of this...")
6. She identifies as curious and intellectually driven, describing herself as a scientist. (Verbatim: "I'm a scientist i'm a i am curious like this is not like the thirst for knowledge i still managed to discover league of legends...")
7. She has a strong connection to the internet, stating she was "basically raised by a computer and a cat." (Verbatim: "i'm like basically raised by a computer and a cat")
8. She has not used Twitter prior to becoming a VTuber and finds it an "interesting place" with both positive and negative aspects. (Verbatim: "i've never been on twitter really to be honest like i never had like was it just never on twitter until until like being vtuber it was like i just didn't know much about twitter like at all")
9. She is aware of internet culture but claims to have avoided "weird places" online. (Verbatim: "apparently there's some really weird places but i don't i don't know i don't know about them and people won't heckin tell me because it's like you don't need to know you don't need to know")
10. She has a playful, self-aware sense of humor about her own vocabulary and online language use. (Verbatim: "i just i don't know even though i spend time on the internet the street language yeah the streets of the internet i i'm still uh learning about yeah") [end of text]



1. She is not French despite common misconceptions. (Verbatim: "I'm not French though. Don't confuse people!")
2. She has a British accent that is distinct and described as "a farmer kind of accent" hidden since childhood. (Verbatim: "My accent is a farmer kind of accent that's been like hidden since I was younger.")
3. She was taught to speak with a more formal, "BBC-style" accent to avoid appearing working class. (Verbatim: "I was always told that I needed to pronounce my t's and don't pronounce my r's harshly.")
4. She had a traumatic childhood experience where a friend destroyed her favorite Pokémon movie poster. (Verbatim: "She tore it more and then I got more upset and she was just laughing and then she went to tear it more and more and more to make me cry and cry and cry.")
5. She has a deep emotional attachment to Pokémon: The First Movie and carried a backpack with it as a child. (Verbatim: "I had this tiny tiny tiny backpack... I would only keep one thing in this backpack: Pokémon the first movie.")
6. She struggled with language learning due to her school not offering German or other languages beyond French and Spanish. (Verbatim: "Oh, I would have learned German if I could have, but they didn't offer German at my school.")
7. She took her French GCSE three years early at age 15. (Verbatim: "So normally you would do them in, like, year 10. But I had to do them three years early. So, yeah. So, I am, like, 15 years old, I got to.")
8. She finds the idea of different sign languages confusing and frustrating, especially the existence of multiple systems. (Verbatim: "What's funny is... there's like American sign language and English sign language and I'm like why is there two sign language?")
9. She believes the idea that Japan reads maps upside down is false and finds it absurd. (Verbatim: "They don't read the maps upside down in Japan and I was like, Where the heck you getting this info from me like?")
10. She has a strong dislike for people pretending to know sign language when they don't. (Verbatim: "People that lie about sign language to get on stage, the thing I don't like about sign language...") [end of text]



1. She identifies as British despite being born in Germany. (Verbatim: "although I was born in Germany I was raised in England um yeah so uh Japanese is already hard enough")
2. She was born in Germany and raised in England. (Verbatim: "although I was born in Germany I was raised in England um yeah so uh Japanese is already hard enough")
3. She has British citizenship. (Verbatim: "am I EU citizen no I'm British I have British citizenship")
4. She is learning Japanese and is actively trying to improve her skills. (Verbatim: "but I'm trying to learn Japanese and my brain can only cope with learning like one language at a time so yeah")
5. She plans to visit Japan in October with a group of fellow VTubers including Videro. (Verbatim: "and the four of us are going to Japan in October and we are thinking like you know doing like streams to prepare for it")
6. She is involved in collaborative Japanese language learning streams with other VTubers before her trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "we attempt to do a collab the four of us and we can only speak Japanese like only speak Japanese")
7. She has a strong emotional attachment to her British identity and was upset when it was removed from her wiki page. (Verbatim: "why doesn't it say I'm British on my own wiki guys guys it's like it's like yo it doesn't heck you'd say I'm British I am why does it not say it")
8. She is concerned about being misidentified as German due to her birthplace. (Verbatim: "Germany can claim me oh my goodness do you know the amount of times in my life where like okay so I get I get id'd always for everything um cry but because of because of my id it'll say like country of birth like um and the country of birth will say Germany")
9. She has taken language lessons in German in the past but fell behind. (Verbatim: "so it was like a term so I did a term of lessons and then I fell behind so yeah but I definitely want to do some")
10. She has a fictional title of "Goose of the Caves" created by her community. (Verbatim: "Elia's community created many titles for her like messenger from the stars goose of the caves menace to the koroks chatium attic tangent incarnate yonker of hearts queen of the banana republic") [end of text]



1. She has a strong connection to children, having worked as a teaching assistant for primary school students. (Verbatim: "I was like a teaching assistant for like a um for like a primary school so we're talking like six seven year olds")
2. She received 30 wedding proposals from young children during her time as a teaching assistant. (Verbatim: "I got like I don't know like in 30 30 wedding proposals from a bunch of small children")
3. She is skilled at mimicking sounds and noises, particularly in interactions with young children. (Verbatim: "apparently i'm very good at making noises because like i just reciprocate the noises that she did to me")
4. She has a large collection of plushies, including a two-meter-tall goose plush and two designated "plushie mountains." (Verbatim: "i have a two meter goose plush on my bed" and "i have plushie mountain one and plushie mountain two")
5. She is currently planning to move out of her current residence in June due to lack of space for VR setup. (Verbatim: "i have to move out of my place in like june but um but i was thinking i gotta make sure that wherever i move to i gotta make sure i have like space")
6. She has lived in England her entire life and has never experienced living elsewhere. (Verbatim: "i've always lived in england um i wonder what it's like to live elsewhere")
7. She is not a very "homely" person but is known for getting along well with children. (Verbatim: "i'm not a very like homey kind of person like homely whatever like person I guess you know but but apparently I get along really well with children")
8. She once forgot her screwdriver at university and had to use a knife to complete tasks requiring screwdrivers. (Verbatim: "i forgot to bring my screwdriver with me my my trusty screwdriver and it was just one year because like the other years i always remember but i remember one year i just forgot")
9. She has a habit of using the phrase "righty tighty, lefty lucy" when referring to screwing or unscrewing objects. (Verbatim: "righty tighty and lefty lucy but the problem with that rule is i don't know my lefts and rights")
10. She has a playful, self-deprecating sense of humor about her lack of spatial awareness and direction. (Verbatim: "i know east because i'm west because because you just i know even though i don't know left and right") [end of text]



1. She has long hair. (Verbatim: "I've got long hair and the water is too cold pain and then like sometimes it wasn't always 10 minutes")
2. She struggled with cold water during childhood, particularly in England. (Verbatim: "the water in england is freezing next level cold and yeah i got kicked out of that surf class pretty much even before they could figure out i couldn't really swim")
3. She has experienced near-drowning incidents at least twice. (Verbatim: "there are two times where i've almost drowned i really should just not be in the water")
4. She is afraid of cold temperatures and gets cold easily. (Verbatim: "i get cold very easily um i don't like being cold i'm like the kind of person where like does anyone ever get so cold that you just don't you don't you don't move like you literally just you you literally freeze")
5. She has difficulty with swimming and relies on floaties for reassurance. (Verbatim: "i can kind of swim but i like having floaties just for the reassurance that i don't drown you know i know i look stupid but i'd rather look stupid than be dead")
6. She had a limited hot water supply at her parents' house, with only 10 minutes of hot water per shower. (Verbatim: "there's only ever 10 minutes of hot water at a time yeah yeah yeah so once it hit 10 minutes you would get like the coldest ice cold shower ever")
7. She remembers using a timer to track her shower time due to the limited hot water. (Verbatim: "i used to actually have a timer that i would keep up just so i would know because the the saddest thing would be like imagine like your hair like with shampoo or conditioner that you need to wash out again")
8. She has a strong emotional connection to the experience of taking long showers. (Verbatim: "the joy of being able to take a shower that's longer than 10 minutes like whoa like")
